  "id": "COMPOUND:29220 - PROTEIN:4951",
  "verbalization": "Cryptophycin G is implicated in the biological activity against HL-60 cells through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Cryptophycin G targets Lysine-specific demethylase 2A, which is then a target of multiple compounds, including (2R)-2-[4-(7-Chloroquinoxalin-2-Yl)Oxyphenoxy]Propanoic Acid, Megastigma-4,6(Z),8(Z)-triene, and Notoamide I. All these compounds ultimately act on HL-60 cells, indicating a potential pathway where Cryptophycin G may exert its effects through the modulation of Lysine-specific demethylase 2A, which in turn influences the cellular response in HL-60 cells. The shared target of these compounds at Lysine-specific demethylase 2A suggests a common mechanism of action, possibly involving the regulation of epigenetic processes. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Lysine-specific demethylase 2A as a critical node in the interaction network between Cryptophycin G and HL-60 cells, reinforcing the possibility of a direct or indirect relationship between the drug and the cell line.",
